{
 "doc": "Plan 062-3a, criterion 4.1, measured 2026-10-26 before deleting the classic ground. Mean colour (before light and fog) of the role sheets assets/original/themes/<god>/roles/<role>.png weighted by each map's ground_roles.png, against (a) the classic ground it replaces (themes/<god>/atlas.png weighted by assets/original/maps/<map>/tiles.png, the ids translated to James's land) and (b) what the original paints on each map of the god's own land (its own TMAP ids on its own land's MAPTs). Cells with tile id 0 (the void filler) count on neither side. Wanted: |d saturation| <= 0.03, |d value| <= 0.03, |d hue| <= 4 deg. test_flat and test_flat4 have no tiles (all open): nothing to compare.",
 "how": {
  "classic": "python3 -I tools/import/measure_ground.py --roles=assets/original/themes/<god>/roles --map=scenes/map/maps/<map>/ground_roles.png --atlas=assets/original/themes/<god>/atlas.png --weights=assets/original/maps/<map>/tiles.png (the atlases are deleted in 062-3d: this file is the record)",
  "original": "SAC_INSTALL=... python3 -I tools/import/bake_role_sheets.py --god=<god> --measure"
 },
 "decision": "GroundRole.tint stays white in the five gods. Against the original every own-land map passes (7 of 7 with Persephone's two). Against the classic 23 of 28 god x map pairs fail, every one by the classic's double translation (map ids -> James -> the god's groups by height band: Pyro's open showed its earth, Charnel's open its pale rim and rock, Peaks read as snow), the defect plan 062 removes; a tint that matched it would move the ground away from the original (Charnel on Peaks: classic value 0.89, original 0.58). Two fixes in the sheets came out of this measure: Charnel's open (32 tiles) keeps the tiles its maps paint most (fit_cells), and Charnel's path, which its land lacks, borrows MG02 (sheet_borrow in ground_roles_table.json).",
