  "doc": "2026-10-26, after the 062-3 playtest (loose pale squares on Charnel, light and dark diamonds on Pyro's plateau). Cause: a role made of groups that look different (Charnel open = MG03 pale spawn pockets V0.61 + MG04 brown V0.40; Pyro earth = MG01 V0.69 + MG02 V0.84; Stratos earth = MG03 + MG04) mixed their tiles in one 4x4 sheet, and the shader picks one cell at random per 10 m cell, so the odd tile showed as a loose square (Charnel: fit_cells gave MG03's tile 30 one cell of 16). In the original those groups lie in their own height bands and never mix cell by cell. Fix: bake_role_sheets.one_look keeps, per role, the most painted group plus the groups that pass plan 062's colour criterion against it (measure_ground.same_look); the table keeps every group's role on the map.",
