  "brightness": "The in-match change against the pre-062-3 ground (luminance of the fixed boxes: Peaks overview -38 %, Roads overview -28 %, Pyro on High Noon plateau -46 %, Winter Wonder ground +46 %) is not the sheets: their colour before light matches the original (above). Two causes, both toward the original: the classic atlas showed other groups (double id translation: Charnel on Peaks classic V0.89 vs original 0.58, Winter Wonder grey), and the classic shader never applied the map's baked light (GroundSet.lightmap_tint 0), which the original does (sacengine dagon terrain2.d:205-206: 0.5*diffuse*(1+detail)*LMAP). NO VERIFICADO: the lit colour against the running original (it cannot run here) and the LMAP channel order (import_map.py reads bytes 0..2 as RGB, as sacengine maps.d:82 does; Roads then gets a blue light (144,180,252), BGR would give a warm one). Decided 2026-10-27 by the user: LMAP stays RGB, as sacengine reads it."
